      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most equitable method will depend on your city's core priorities, but a pure income-based system is the most direct way to achieve social equity. Prioritizing transit hubs is a good urban planning goal, but it risks creating segregated housing if not balanced with need. A lottery system is inherently random and ignores the urgent needs of the most vulnerable populations. Therefore, a tiered system that heavily weights income need while perhaps offering a small preference for transit access is a balanced approach.",
      "source": "target",
